\subsection{On internationality in mathematical oncology}
\label{sec:internationality}
%
We next set out to study how international mathematical oncology is by analysing author affiliation countries in article metadata.
%
The box plots in Figure \ref{fig:internationality}a show how many affiliation countries are represented per article, and how these numbers have changed over time since 1967, the first year with available affiliation data. 
%

To situate our results for mathematical oncology* articles in a broader context, we also generate the corresponding box plots for the mathematical biology* (excluding mathematical oncology*) dataset. 
