The latter box plot, with the larger dataset, demonstrates a clear correlation between country numbers and citation counts: in 46 out of 58 boxes, articles with above-average citation counts have a higher mean number of affiliation countries than articles with below-average citation counts. Only in 11 boxes is the reverse true, which motivates international collaborations. 
