 \begin{proof}
    For $R\geq \L(g_1,g_2)$, recall from previous Section \ref{section, PreliminaryLipMaps} that the sets $ \Lip_{id}(M,g_1,g_2) $ and $\mathcal{A}_R$ are convex.
 Take two maps $\varphi_0$ and $\varphi_1$ in $\mathcal{A}_R$ and connect them by a geodesic $\psi_s$  as in Proposition \ref{prop,convexityLip}. By Proposition \ref{prop,convexityLength},
$$ L_{g_2} ( \psi_s(c_{v}^{g_1}[0,1])) \leq s \cdot L_{g_2} ( \varphi_0(c_{v}^{g_1} [0,1])  +(1-s)L_{g_2} ( \varphi_1(c_{v}^{g_1} [0,1]) $$
for all $v \in S^{g_1}M$. Choose $m  \in\mathcal{M}^{1}(\phi^{g_1})$. The integration with respect to the probability measure $m$ yields

$$G(\psi_s,m) \leq s G(\varphi_0,m) +(1-s) G(\varphi_1,m).$$

%The map  $ f\to G(f,\mu_0)$ is lower semi-continuous from Lemma \ref{lem,correctCompactness}.
