\section{Analysis Results}
\subsection{Malware Distribution}
On November 13, 2024, an attempted social engineering attack was detected involving \textit{LinkedIn}, a widely trusted professional networking platform. The target, a Web3 and blockchain developer, was approached by an individual posing as a representative of a reputable company in the NFT and blockchain space. The attacker initially framed their approach as a business opportunity, inviting the target to participate in an NFT gaming project, as extensively reported by Luca Di Domenico on his \href{https://lucadidomenico.notion.site/Someone-tried-to-rug-me-on-Linkedin-13d8b714b46c80968c32c77737287e54}{Notion website}.

