\textit{Anti-debugging} and \textit{Anti-Tampering} techniques are also employed. The script includes functions designed to detect if it is being debugged and alter its behavior, accordingly, potentially interfering with debugging efforts, by even invoking the \textit{debugger} statement dynamically, which can cause debuggers to pause execution unexpectedly or enter infinite loops.

