\textit{Confusing naming conventions} are also used as a decoy strategy. The use of similar or repeating variable names with slight variations, such as \textbf{\textit{\_0x214ade}} and \textbf{\textit{\_0x2f409e}}, can cause confusion. This practice makes it difficult to track variables and understand their roles in the code.

