Starting from the main execution point, the script begins by importing necessary modules and setting up the environment. It attempts to import critical libraries required for its operation, and if they are not present, it installs them using \textit{pip} to ensure all dependencies are met. This includes libraries for \textit{HTTP requests}, cryptographic functions, and OS-specific modules for accessing system resources.

