The script then saves the (possibly modified) configuration files to the attacker's server. By calling \textbf{\textit{save\_conf()}}, the script reads the contents of \textit{conf\_path1} and \textit{conf\_path2} and sends them to the server, allowing the attacker to retrieve the configuration files. Finally, the script restarts \textit{AnyDesk} and deletes itself.

