We also found two cluster 2 (dimer) phases, both in general assuming the form of oblique lattices. In the first, dimers are oriented along the line equidistant to neighboring dimers — described by the angle $\phi=\arctan( b\sin\theta/(a+b\cos\theta) )$ — referred to here as the {\it oblique cluster 2 lattice}, or simply Cluster 2. In the second, the dimers align along a primitive direction of the oblique lattice, referred to as the {\it oblique cluster 2-aligned lattice}, or just Cluster 2a. Additionally, we identified a {\it honeycomb} lattice, corresponding to a cluster 2 ``inverse micelle'' or ``hole''-type phase. The specific ansatz for these are illustrated in the second row of Fig.~\ref{fig:specific_ansatz}.


