\section{Proof of Theorem \ref{pro}}
\label{th1_proof_apendix}

We define $\rm{SNR} \triangleq \frac{P_t}{\sigma_w^2}$ with $P_t = \mathbb{E}[s[k]^2]$ denoting the transmit signal power. The signal power of $s_{n,m}$ can be calculated as follows

\begin{align}
    \nonumber \mathbb{E}[\bm{\varphi}_{n,m} \bm{\varphi}_{n,m}^*] &= \mathbb{E}[(\mathbf{H}_{n,m}[:,D']s_{n,m})^H (\mathbf{H}_{n,m}[:,D']s_{n,m})] \\ \nonumber  &= P_t ||\mathbf{H}_{n,m}[:,D']||^2.
\end{align}

We know that the symbols in the DD Domain are independent of each other. Due to the unitary transformation characteristic of IDFT, the samples in the time Domain are also uncorrelated of each other, which means

\begin{align}
    \mathbb{E}[s_{n,i}s_{n,j}^*] = P_t \delta[i-j],
\end{align}

where $\delta[\cdot]$ denotes the Kronecker delta function. The calculation of noise plus interference power is shown in Equation (\ref{eq:prove_noise}) which completes the proof of Theorem \ref{pro}.

