In this way, we may assume $j_1 \le j_2 \dots \le j_{2m}$ in exchange for reordering $S_{i_1}, \dots, S_{i_m}$. That is, if suffices to consider graphs of the form
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.7, baseline=(current bounding box.center)]
    \coordinate[vtx] (v0) at (0, 2);
    \node at (v0) [above] {$\tilde{S}_{j_1}$};
    \coordinate[vtx] (v1) at (1.5, 2);
    \node at (v1) [above] {$\tilde{S}_{j_2}$};
    \coordinate[vtx] (u0) at (0, 0);
    \node at (u0) [below] {$S_{i_{\phi(1)}}$};
    \coordinate[vtx] (u1) at (1.5, 0);
    \node at (u1) [below] {$S_{i_{\phi(2)}}$};
