Applying this to the joint decomposition then yields {\footnotesize \begin{align*}
    &\ip{e_{a}(\xg),\mu(\xg)}_{L^2(\ta\backslash \{t_r\},\lambda) \oplus \ell^2(\{t_r\})} \\
    &= \ip{e_{a},\mu}_{L^2(\ta\backslash \{t_r\},\lambda) \oplus \ell^2(\{t_r\})}
