    \item The policyholder then makes a withdrawal $w(t_k)$ at time $t_k$. The policyholder may choose not to make a withdrawal at this time, in which case we have $w(t_k) = 0$. The maximum possible withdrawal is the maximum between the post-fee investment account value $X(t_k^-)(1-\varphi \Delta t)$ and the guaranteed withdrawal amount $g(t_k)$. That is,$$0 \leq w(t_k) \leq \max\{X(t_k^-)(1-\varphi \Delta t), g(t_k)\}, \qquad k=1,2,\dots,N.$$

