\section{Objective Function with Excess Withdrawal Penalty and Option to ``Toggle'' the Cash Fund}

This appendix states the policyholder's total discounted cash flows when there is a proportional penalty for excess withdrawals and an option to forego the cash fund. Let $\vm{1}_{CF}$ be an indicator function with value 1 if the contract includes a cash fund and with value 0 otherwise. Furthermore, let $\zeta \in [0,1]$ denote an excess withdrawal penalty: if the policyholder withdraws an amount $w(t_k) > g(t_k)$, then the amount they actually receive is reduced by $\zeta(w(t_k) - g(t_k))$.\footnote{In \citet{Moenig-2016}, for example, the excess withdrawal penalty is called the surrender penalty.} The withdrawal amount net of the excess withdrawal penalty is therefore $w(t_k) - \zeta(w(t_k) - g(t_k))^+$. Furthermore, the post-tax value of the net withdrawal is \[\text{post-tax withdrawal} = (1 - \theta) (w(t_k) - \zeta(w(t_k) - g(t_k))^+).\]

In the taxation scheme assumed in this paper, the interest earnings on the cash fund are taxed, but not the actual balance of the cash fund itself. Consider the cash fund injection, if any, at time $t_k$. If $w(t_k) < g(t_k)$, then the amount $g(t_k) - w(t_k)$ is deposited into the cash fund, where it will earn interest at a rate $\eta$ over the period $[t_k, t_N]$. The interest earned, given by \[(e^{\eta(t_N - t_k)} - 1) (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+\] is then subject to the marginal tax rate $\theta$. Therefore, the contribution of the injection at time $t_k$ to the terminal value of the cash fund is \[\underbrace{(1 - \theta) (e^{\eta(t_N - t_k)} - 1) (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+}_{\text{post-tax interest income on CF}} + (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+.\] This expression can be simplified to $[(1 - \theta) e^{\eta (t_N - t_k)} + \theta] (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+.$

Therefore, given an admissible withdrawal strategy $\vm{w} \in \mathcal{W}$ and the corresponding trajectories of the VA investment account value $\vm{X}$ and the benefit base $\vm{G}$ achieved under the withdrawal strategy $\vm{w}$, the discounted value at time $t = 0$ of all cash flows from the VA contract is
\begin{align*}
    H_0(\vm{X}, \vm{G}, \vm{w})
        & = \sum_{k=1}^{N-1} e^{-r t_k} (1 - \theta) \left(w(t_k) - \zeta(w(t_k) - g(t_k))^+\right) \\
        & \qquad + e^{-r t_N} \vm{1}_{CF} \sum_{k=1}^{N-1} \Big( [(1 - \theta) e^{\eta (t_N - t_k)} + \theta] (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+ \Big) \\
        & \qquad + e^{-r t_N} (1 - \theta) \max \{X^{PF}(t_N^-), g(t_N)\}.
\end{align*}
The second summation can be written as follows
\begin{align*}
    & e^{-r t_N} \vm{1}_{CF} \sum_{k=1}^{N-1} \Big( [(1 - \theta) e^{\eta (t_N - t_k)} + \theta] (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+ \Big) \\
    & \qquad = e^{-r t_N} \vm{1}_{CF} \sum_{k=1}^{N-1} e^{-r t_k} e^{r t_k} [(1 - \theta) e^{\eta (t_N - t_k)} + \theta] (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+ \\
    & \qquad = \sum_{k=1}^{N-1} \vm{1}_{CF} e^{-r t_k}  e^{-r (t_N - t_k)} [(1 - \theta) e^{\eta (t_N - t_k)} + \theta] (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+ \\
    & \qquad = \sum_{k=1}^{N-1} \vm{1}_{CF} e^{-r t_k} \left[(1 - \theta) e^{-(r - \eta) (t_N - t_k)} + \theta e^{-r (t_N - t_k)}\right] (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+
\end{align*}
The total discounted cash flows can therefore be written as \[H_0(\vm{X}, \vm{G}, \vm{w}) = \sum_{k=1}^{N-1} e^{-r t_k} C(t_k, X(t_k^-), G(t_k^-), w(t_k)) + e^{-r t_N} D(X(t_N^-), G(t_N^-)),\] where
\begin{align*}
    C(t_k, X(t_k^-), G(t_k^-), w(t_k))
        & := (1 - \theta) \left(w(t_k) - \zeta(w(t_k) - g(t_k))^+\right) \\
        & \qquad + \vm{1}_{CF} \left[(1 - \theta) e^{-(r - \eta) (t_N - t_k)} + \theta e^{-r (t_N - t_k)}\right] (g(t_k) - w(t_k))^+ \\
    D(X(t_N^-), G(t_N^-))
        & := (1 - \theta) \max \{X^{PF}(t_N^-), g(t_N)\}.
\end{align*}
From equations \eqref{eqn-Update-InvestmentAccount-PostFee} and \eqref{eqn-GuaranteedWithdrawalAmount}, we note that the right-hand sides of $C(t_k, X(t_k^-), G(t_k^-), w(t_k))$ and $D(X(t_N^-), G(t_N^-))$ are indeed functions of $X(t_k^-)$ and $G(t_k^-)$.

\begin{rem}
    If $\zeta = 0$ (no excess withdrawal penalty), $\theta = 0$ (no tax), and $\vm{1}_{CF} = 1$ (policyholder has a cash fund), then we obtain the base case specified by equations \eqref{eqn-TotalDiscountedCF-Running} and \eqref{eqn-TotalDiscountedCF-Terminal}.
\end{rem}

