are the row and column variance matrices, which means for each $\Yibf$, the covariance between row $i,j$ is $(\Sigmabf_0)_{ij}$ and the the covariance between column $k,l$ is $(\Psibf_0)_{kl}$. Also, we let $\Omegabf_{0}=\Sigmabf_{0}^{-1} $ and $ \Gammabf_{0}=\Psibf_{0}^{-1}  $ be the precision matrices for row and column vectors, respectively.
