\section*{Appendix - Proof of Theorem 4.1}\label{appn}

We first show that $\hat{\Sigmabf}_H$ is unbiased for $\Sigmabf_0$. Note
that 
$$
E_{P_0} \left[{\bf Y}_{1} {\bf Y}_{1}^{\top}\right]=\sum_{j=1}^{q} E_{P_0} \left[ ({\bf Y}_{1})_{:j} ({\bf Y}_{1})_{:j}^{\top} \right],
$$

\noindent
where $({\bf Y}_{1})_{:j}$ denotes the $j^{th}$ column of ${\bf Y}_1$. 
Note that for any $1 \leqslant k \leqslant p$ and $1 \leqslant l \leqslant p$, the $(k,l)^{th}$ 
entry of $E_{P_0} \left[ ({\bf Y}_{1})_{:j} ({\bf Y}_{1})_{:j}^{\top} \right]$ 
is given by
\begin{eqnarray*}
E_{P_0} \left[\left(Y_{1}\right)_{k j}\left(Y_{1}\right)_{l j}\right]=\left(\Sigma_{0}\right)_{k l}\left(\Psi_{0}\right)_{j j}. 
\end{eqnarray*}

\noindent
It follows that 
$$
